#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "15c029df-b002-51cc-87db-a94d40a02771" :question/math-academy-id "e-595" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad 0\\leq t<2\\pi$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/0f8bfc82b98e63e586e9d2e96d1acc5d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "148e5378-9177-59ba-9b1e-3633c940babd" :question/math-academy-id "e-596" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty$,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} & = \\frac{- {e}^{- t}}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{t}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{2 t}} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1$, the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} |}_{t = 1} & = - \\frac{1}{{e}^{2 ( 1 )} ( 1 + 1 )} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{2 {e}^{2}} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a138017d-47fa-598d-a933-92367eee3825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082317} {:answer/id #uuid "b6dbfd57-bd52-5653-9348-bec77c8949d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082318} {:answer/id #uuid "e3adecf5-9d81-5833-a254-fb447b141534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082319} {:answer/id #uuid "3534a217-beb4-51f9-b215-8e2b858e9868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082320} {:answer/id #uuid "3a833825-f97a-5e8b-8374-759b0958c9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3534a217-beb4-51f9-b215-8e2b858e9868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082320} :answer-field/id #uuid "7866304e-1f46-5cfd-ba9b-9131acf20f8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082316}] :question/id #uuid "a73a45f9-70e6-5c98-9255-49149400966d" :question/math-academy-id "q-6808" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/q-6808.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve\n$x = 4\\cos t, y = 3\\sin 2t, 0 \\le t < 2\\pi $,\nshown above, calculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t = \\frac{\\pi }{6}$."}]}
